{"id": "EUVD-2026-101062", "enisaUuid": "5ef432bf-7983-3fce-ad15-f2ba7aa419e5", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nselinux: always fill AVC decision in avc_has_perm_noaudit()\n\navc_has_perm_noaudit() is documented to return a copy of the access\ndecision in @avd, but its early return for an empty requested permission\nset leaves the buffer untouched.  All callers pass an uninitialized\nstack variable and afterwards feed it to avc_audit(), and the inode hook\neven stores it in the per-task decision cache.\n\nFill in a deny-all, audit-all decision, similar to avd_init(), so every\ncaller receives a defined value at no cost on the hot path.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T13:27:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c781e737aa0de95289b1774d5fd29388895737a9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e308c5acfe283a66627fc407065626df4ab753ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f9da796fa238f8e4414ee8481e6c979759a3d563", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e77461af13eab5c9a953cc52ec8432cc941d61e2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5a6f9a872b4ff68877caf998bee352153b7154bc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24e00850bcff46b984f4c44b92e5499450fcfb5a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/835133337c2ce200db56f62d018c79087dee2603", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8861db305103107199b1426f25fde1fb6d465583"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98413", "GHSA-m3f9-pmfc-6c92"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "08157b3d-ab24-3409-884b-512edc65f7fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e6f2f381e4015386a656a369835f949c26000e6b <e77461af13eab5c9a953cc52ec8432cc941d61e2"}, {"id": "1b0ba6c5-d572-36b0-8e6d-8095b2648ff0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "e6f2f381e4015386a656a369835f949c26000e6b <f9da796fa238f8e4414ee8481e6c979759a3d563"}, {"id": "356761bb-6a28-3bbe-b5a9-c966984b9487", 